SIMPLE  =                    T / file does conform to FITS standard             BITPIX  =                   16 / number of bits per data pixel                  NAXIS   =                    0 / number of data axes                            EXTEND  =                    T / FITS dataset may contain extensions            COMMENT   FITS (Flexible Image Transport System) format is defined in 'AstronomyCOMMENT   and Astrophysics', volume 376, page 359; bibcode: 2001A&A...376..359H TELESCOP= 'BURSTCUBE'          / Telescope (mission) name                       INSTRUME= 'CS0     '           / Instrument Name                                ORIGIN  = 'GSFC    '           / Source of FITS file                            CCLS0001= 'BCF     '           / Basic Calibration File                         CDTP0001= 'DATA    '           / Calibration file contains data                 CCNM0001= 'ALIGNMENT'          / Type of calibration file                       CVSD0001= '2021-01-01'         / UTC date when file should first be used        CVST0001= '00:00:00'           / UTC time when file should first be used        CDES0001= 'DETECTOR ORIENTATION' / Brief descriptive summary of this file       ALIGNM11=   0.7071067811865475 / Component of the alignment matrix              ALIGNM12=                 -0.5 / Component of the alignment matrix              ALIGNM13=                 -0.5 / Component of the alignment matrix              ALIGNM21=   0.7071067811865475 / Component of the alignment matrix              ALIGNM22=                  0.5 / Component of the alignment matrix              ALIGNM23=                  0.5 / Component of the alignment matrix              ALIGNM31=                  0.0 / Component of the alignment matrix              ALIGNM32=  -0.7071067811865475 / Component of the alignment matrix              ALIGNM33=   0.7071067811865475 / Component of the alignment matrix              ROLLSIGN=                    1 / Sign of roll positive direction about boresightROLLOFF =                  0.0 / Offset of roll angle in degrees                DATE    = '2022-07-26T15:47:27' / File creation date (YYYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss UT)   CHECKSUM= 'oeLVpeKUoeKUoeKU'   / HDU checksum updated 2024-09-15T23:46:31       DATASUM = '0       '           / data unit checksum updated 2022-07-26T10:47:27 COMMENT ----------------------------------------------------------------------- COMMENT This file contains a matrix that serves to transforms a coordinate from COMMENT the detector reference frame (DET) to the spacecraft coordinate         COMMENT system (SAT):                                                           COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT       SATX = M11*DETX + M12*DETY + M13*DETZ                             COMMENT       SATY = M21*DETX + M22*DETY + M23*DETZ                             COMMENT       SATZ = M31*DETX + M32*DETY + M33*DETZ                             COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT The spacecraft coordinate frame is centered in the BurstCube            COMMENT instrument:                                                             COMMENT - the z-axis points towards the boresight of the instrument,            COMMENT - the y-axis points towards the solar panels, and                       COMMENT - the x-axis follows a right-handed convention.                         COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT The BurstCube detectors are arranged in a square pyramidal shape,       COMMENT each facing 45deg from vertical. They are fixed to the spacecraft       COMMENT frame and their orientation does not change.                            COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT - Detector CS0 is located in the -x,+y quadrant.                        COMMENT - Detector CS1 is located in the -x,-y quadrant.                        COMMENT - Detector CS2 is located in the +x,-y quadrant.                        COMMENT - Detector CS3 is located in the +x,+y quadrant.                        COMMENT ----------------------------------------------------------------------- END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             